HTML 

Interesting facts 
.its not a programming language - its a markup language designed to structure and present content on the web
.its everywhere - besides web browsers, its also in many applications, email clients, and even mobile apps 
.its platform independent - it can run on any platform or browser, making it incredibly versatile and universally accessible 
.its case insensitive - lowercase is preferred for consistency
.no closing tags for some elements - self closing 
.semantic elements exist to improve content organization and accessibility 
.its still evolving 
.APIs - it supports several powerful APIs
    .geolocation API to access user location 
    .canvas API for drawing graphics and animations 
    .web storage for storing data locally in the browser 
.comments - can be added, always, anytime 
.custom elements - it allows developers to create their own custom tags using Web Components, providing flexibility and reusability
.as an Art - its used with CSS to create ASCII art or intricate designs, showcasing its creative potential beyond 
functionality
